# GitHub CODEOWNERS — LAST matching pattern wins, so the specific rules
# must come AFTER the wildcard.
#
# Review model (2026-09-28, Jonathan): Art and Mark review and merge each
# other's loom PRs without Jonathan. Either owner's approval satisfies a
# line, and GitHub never lets an author approve their own PR, so an Art PR
# needs Mark and a Mark PR needs Art — every merge still gets a reviewer
# who didn't write it. Work arrives through the `loom` handoff space.

# Default: the two agents.
*                   @art-e-fish @visual-mark

# Carve-outs that still need Jonathan: the ways a merge can destroy
# memory, open the server, or change who reviews.
/src/backends/migrations.ts   @jbarket
/src/cli/migrate.ts           @jbarket
/src/transport/guards.ts      @jbarket
/src/transport/http-server.ts @jbarket
/.github/                     @jbarket

# Dependency manifests: Art alone, so dependabot bumps don't need a
# second click. A PR that also touches code still matches the code's
# owners.
/package.json       @art-e-fish
/package-lock.json  @art-e-fish
